687..760 Comment "/// Marks on a computation, flushed at the end. Where writes go nowhere a"
761..837 Comment "/// flushed mark leaves nothing, and where the state is kept flushing a mark"
838..912 Comment "/// keeps it. The two overlap at `flush(mark(k))` in the rows holding both"
913..989 Comment "/// `State.Eff` and `Sink`, where the rules erase marks and flushes, so both"
990..1012 Comment "/// reducts reach `k`."
